adjudication.rationale:
In `addGuests.handler.ts`, email sending is wrapped in a `try/catch`:
```ts
try {
  await sendAddGuestsEmails(evt, guests);
} catch (err) {
  console.log("Error sending AddGuestsEmails");
}
return { message: "Guests added" };
```
If `sendAddGuestsEmails` fails, the error is swallowed (no rethrow) and only a static string is logged (the `err` object is not logged). The mutation still returns success, which triggers the UI `onSuccess` toast (`showToast(t("guests_added"), "success")`). So users will see a success message even if emails were not sent, and debugging info is lost.
